# Fast lane first: lint-staged formats and auto-fixes only what you actually staged.
npx lint-staged

# Then the two lanes that CANNOT be narrowed to staged files, so they run whole:
#   - tsc typechecks the program, not a file list — an edit here can break a type over there.
#   - a test in one file can fail because of an edit in another.
# Both are ~1s on this package. When the total passes ~5s, move `npm test` to a pre-push hook
# rather than making this smarter: a slow hook gets bypassed with --no-verify, and a bypassed gate
# is worse than no gate because it still feels like one.
npm run --silent typecheck
npm run --silent test
